    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key exactly as specified, keeping structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **New `util/Soundex.java`** \u2014 an isolated, self-contained American Soundex encoder (`Soundex.of(name)`). Putting it in its own tiny class means its inherent branchiness doesn't inflate the WMC of any class other functions must be edited against.\n\n2. **`util/IdentityKey.of`** \u2014 now returns the lower-case SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously the plaintext `telephone|email|`). The existing `telephone()`/`email()` normalizers are reused; a small private `sha256Hex` helper does the digest. `rejectIfDuplicate` is unchanged and still drives the 409, still skipping deleted owners. The email-domain blocklist already runs before duplicate detection in the controller, so that ordering is preserved.\n\n3. **`util/PossibleDuplicate.matchId`** \u2014 the soft match now triggers when `soundex(lastName)` and postcode match but the identity keys differ, instead of the old \"same last name + different telephone\" rule. The now-unused `digits` helper was removed.\n\n**Behavioural results, per spec:**\n- Duplicate 409 is driven solely by the single identity key.\n- Two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** now get different identity keys \u2192 no 409; they're flagged as a soft match instead.\n- The separate household-duplicate 409 path is untouched and remains unwired in the controller (it was already not invoked), so it no longer applies.\n\nThe mapper (`OwnerMapper`) consumes `IdentityKey.of` via an unchanged signature, so no other code needed touching.",
